error[NK2202]: `make` is `sync`, but the cleanup of `_r`, `Res::cleanup`, can pause.
   --> tests/a_pausing_cleanup_in_a_sync_function_is_nk2202.nika:30:5
    |
 30 |     let _r = Res { name: "a" }
    |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    |
    = note: A `sync` function promises never to pause or do I/O.
    = note: `_r` is cleaned up where it dies in `make`, and `Res::cleanup` doesn't say `sync`.
    = help: Remove `sync` from `make`, write `sync` after the signature of `Res::cleanup` if it never pauses, or create `_r` outside `make` and pass it in.
